  "prediction": "G1 passes, at a residual LARGER than the 0.030 the 40-step instrument run showed, because the rotor's own wake deepens over a longer horizon and the whole residual is the gap between the ring the disk reads and the cell its force sits in. G2 and G3 pass. G4 resolves all three joins. G5 returns ADD rather than COMPOUND, because two of the three joins are one-way and the third is algebraic, so there is no loop for an error to go round -- and COMPOUND would have been the more valuable result, since it is Claim B failing at vehicle scale, which f1-pathmap-and-end-goal section 7 calls the most likely failure on the ladder.",
